  "thumbnailAlt": "Trivia Quiz form beside a photo of friends playing a board game around a table",
  "content": {
    "intro": "A trivia quiz is a form that asks multiple-choice or short-answer general knowledge questions and scores each answer, so hosts can run a fun competition and players see how much they know. This template has ten tested questions across science, geography, history and the arts, with quiz mode grading every entry automatically.",
    "audience": "Pub and bar quiz hosts, teachers, team leads running Friday socials, libraries and community groups.",
    "useCases": [
      "A weekly trivia night where teams answer on their phones by QR code",
      "A remote team social or virtual happy hour",
      "A classroom warm-up or end-of-term quiz",
      "A newsletter or social media challenge with a prize for top scorers"
    ],
    "tips": [
      "Quiz mode grades every submission and shows the score instantly; the pass mark is set to 70%, so seven correct answers count as a pass.",
      "Set an open and close time window in Form Settings so answers only count during the round, then export to Excel to rank teams.",
      "Turn on 'one response per person' with sign-in for competitive quizzes so nobody resubmits after seeing their score."
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "What should a trivia quiz include?",
        "answer": "Eight to twelve questions with one clear correct answer each, a mix of topics (science, geography, history, arts, sport), a mix of easy and harder questions, player or team name, and a way to score and show results."
      },
      {
        "question": "How is the trivia quiz scored?",
        "answer": "Each question has an answer key. When someone submits, quiz mode grades their answers automatically, shows their score straight away, and records it with the response so you can sort by score."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I write my own trivia questions?",
        "answer": "Yes. Copy the template into your free account, replace the questions and options, and set the correct answer for each one. You can also ask the AI form builder to draft a themed round."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do I stop players looking up answers?",
        "answer": "You can't fully prevent it online, but a short open window in Form Settings helps, and so does running the quiz live in a room. Questions that need reasoning rather than a quick search also help."
      }
    ]
  },
